    {
      "title": "[P1] Treat a differing cached identity as a card boundary",
      "body": "When the iframe is preloaded from a widget snapshot whose `resultIdentity` is A, `resultCapabilityIdentity.current` is still null, so a capability-only replay for B is not considered changed here. Without `toolInfo` or a current-lifetime result, the old cached data and local view state remain while B restores—and remain indefinitely if restoration fails; compare against `displayedResultIdentity` as well and reset before hydration. This violates the result boundary and fail-closed requirement in `../../AGENTS.md:28`.",
